  "question": {
    "text": "The number of species trom the following carrying a single lone pair on central atom Xenon is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/70532279-9ad9-4993-b17e-a6bc74e280e6-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 280px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/92821475-3c86-49d5-ace1-59a6294b9b80-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 303px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cddbee3e-13c8-48bf-a50d-fe2f003bad4c.png\" style=\"width: 348px; height: 357px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c4ba35cb-1530-4e17-9497-614f0a9e85d3-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 211px;\" /></p><p>The central <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Xe</mi></math> atom in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> has three bonding domains and one&nbsp;lone pair&nbsp;of electrons. Hence, the&nbsp;electron geometry is tetrahedral and molecular geometry is pyramidal.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is&nbsp;trigonal bipyramidal&nbsp;and the shape is a see-saw.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is in&nbsp;square pyramidal shape.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;have single lone pair on central atom.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
